      "content": "#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <climits>\n#include <omp.h>\n\nint main() {\n    int n, s;\n    std::cin >> n >> s;\n\n    // Flatten matrix into contiguous 1D array for better spatial locality\n    const int np1 = n + 1; // size of prefix sum dimension (extra row/col of zeros)\n    std::vector<int> mat(n * n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            scanf(\"%d\", &mat[i * n + j]);\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Integral image (summed-area table) using long long to avoid overflow\n    std::vector<long long> pref(np1 * np1, 0LL);\n\n    // First pass: horizontal cumulative sums per row\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        long long row_sum = 0;\n        const int base_i = (i + 1) * np1;\n        const int mat_base = i * n;\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            row_sum += mat[mat_base + j];\n            pref[base_i + (j + 1)] = row_sum;\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Second pass: vertical accumulation to complete the integral image\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        const int base_cur = (i + 1) * np1;\n        const int base_prev = i * np1;\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            pref[base_cur + (j + 1)] += pref[base_prev + (j + 1)];\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Search for maximum SxS submatrix sum using OpenMP parallelism\n    long long mxSum = LLONG_MIN;\n    const int limit = n - s;  // inclusive upper bound for starting indices\n\n    #pragma omp parallel for collapse(2) reduction(max:mxSum)\n    for (int i = 0; i <= limit; ++i) {\n        const long long *row_i_s = &pref[(i + s) * np1];\n        const long long *row_i   = &pref[i * np1];\n        for (int j = 0; j <= limit; ++j) {\n            long long sum = row_i_s[j + s] - row_i[j + s]\n                           - row_i_s[j] + row_i[j];\n            if (sum > mxSum) mxSum = sum;\n        }\n    }\n\n    printf(\"%d\\n\", static_cast<int>(mxSum));\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Combining integral image (O(1) submatrix sum), contiguous 1D storage for cache efficiency, and OpenMP parallelization over all starting positions yields the fastest correct solution.",
